planation\": \"双氯芬酸钠肠溶, another NSAID distinct from ibuprofen, is explicitly linked to increased bleeding risk when used with anticoagulants like dicoumarol, with evidence stating that co-administration 'has an increased risk of bleeding.' This aligns with the broader class effect of NSAIDs on hemostasis. The relationship is supported by structured data indicating an INTERACTS_WITH relationship between 双氯芬酸钠肠溶 and 双香豆素, with 凝血酶原时间 implicitly affected due to the described bleeding risk mechanism [Data: Relationships (32126); Entities (4166)]. Although not directly tied to PT in the relationship description, the mechanistic context and parallel phrasing with ibuprofen entries strongly associate it with PT prolongation.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Gastrointestinal bleeding and ulceration are key adverse reactions\",\n            \"explanation\": \"复方布洛芬 is specifically associated with serious gastrointestinal adverse effects, including 胃肠道出血或溃疡 (gastrointestinal bleeding or ulceration). The evidence advises immediate discontinuation and physician consultation if these symptoms occur. This finding underscores a major safety concern inherent to NSAID use, particularly in combination products. Additionally, combining 复方布洛芬 with other 解热镇痛抗炎药 (antipyretic, analgesic, and anti-inflammatory drugs) is warned against due to increased risk of gastrointestinal adverse reactions and potential ulcer development [Data: Relationships (10717, 34645); Entities (4705, 11857)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Contraindications in vulnerable patient populations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Oral hypoglycemic agents (口服降血糖药物) are contraindicated or require extreme caution in specific high-risk populations, including 老年患者 (elderly patients), 肝肾功能低下患者 (patients with impaired liver or kidney function), and 营养不良患者 (malnourished patients). In these groups, drug interactions can lead to exaggerated blood glucose-lowering effects and severe hyp